[[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2891550\">2125C24</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2892286\">7065C10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2892172\">7040A11</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolt.</p><p>2. Move the instrument panel slightly.</p><p>3. Disconnect the electrical connections (3a, 3b, 3c).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3a</p></td><td><p>Instrument panel</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/2890270\">E50C</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3b</p></td><td><p>Instrument panel</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/2890263\">E50B</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3c</p></td><td><p>Instrument panel</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/2890257\">E50A</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2035462.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the instrument panel\nis not damaged.</p><p>If the instrument panel is replaced, renew\nany bridges at the rear so that they are identical to the ones for\nthe panel removed (see &quot;Descriptions and Operation&quot;).</p><p>Connect the electrical connections.</p><p>Refit the instrument panel and fix it using\nthe bolt.</p><p>Check the operation of the instrument and\nthe functions controlled by it.</p><p><a href=\"#/2892286\">7065C10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2892172\">7040A11</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2891550\">2125C24</a></p>"]]